# PERMIT DENIED — project contract

One compact destruction sandbox. Same lot every run. No meta, no campaign, no second map.

**Title** on the window: `PERMIT DENIED`. Internal shorthand “Killdozer” starts out of copy.

## Doc authority

- `README.md` is how to run, keys, and current sandbox scope.
- `assets/usable/ASSETS.md` is the tile/atlas contract.
- `PERMIT_DENIED.md` / `PERMIT_DENIED_GO_IMPLEMENTATION.md` are legacy design notes; prefer the sandbox README when they conflict with cell-based destruction.

## Stack lock

Go 1.25 + Ebitengine **v2.9.x**. Module `permitdenied`. 60 TPS. Logical screen **320×224**; window starts **1280×896**. `Layout` always returns `(320, 224)`.

## Stay on the lot

Tune `internal/game/const.go` before adding a system. A threat that does not change **steering** does not ship.

Keep out of this build: title/campaign/meta, JSON schemas, plugin systems, between-run unlocks, a second lot, soft-body / particle debris **as collision**, ECS, Godot / Raylib / React wrappers.

Buildings are **per-cell** destructible. Visual debris is garnish. Rubble collides and matches its sprite.

Copy: `BLADE UP` / `BLADE DOWN`, deaths `ENGINE COOKED` / `TRACK THROWN` / `COUNTY CLOCK`. Do not write Heemeyer, Granby, manifesto, or wanted stars.

## Done

Sandbox playable with local bites, collapse dust, rubble aftermath, and captured frames that show it. After that holds, stop expanding.
